(a) It shall be disorderly conduct to be found drunk making any unnecessary or unusual noise to the disturbance of any citizen.
(b) It shall be disorderly conduct to use violent, boisterous, profane, or obscene language in public places, use opprobrious words to another or in his presence, without provocation.
(c) An assault or an assault and battery shall constitute disorderly conduct and shall be a misdemeanor.
